# IBVAP — Complete Technical Deep Dive
## Intelligent Border Video Analytics Platform
### SIH 2026 | MHA / BSF | Research-Backed Analysis

---

## SECTION 1: WHAT THIS SYSTEM ACTUALLY IS

### The Core Idea (Plain English)

Border posts today have thousands of standard IP CCTV cameras. They were bought
to record video and let a guard watch a screen. The guard gets tired. The camera
records 24/7 but nobody is watching at 3 AM when something actually happens.

IBVAP replaces the tired guard with an AI layer — a software pipeline that sits
between the existing CCTV cameras and the command center. The cameras stay the
same (no hardware swap). The software receives their video streams via standard
RTSP protocol, runs 6-7 AI models on them in real time, and fires alerts when
something needs a human to look.

```
[Border CCTV Cameras]
        │ RTSP streams (standard IP protocol)
        ▼
[IBVAP Ingestion Layer]  ← Your software starts here
        │
        ▼
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           AI ANALYTICS PIPELINE               │
│                                               │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐            │
│  │ YOLOv8      │  │ DeepSORT /  │            │
│  │ Detector    │→ │ ByteTrack   │            │
│  │ (humans,    │  │ (tracker)   │            │
│  │  vehicles)  │  └─────────────┘            │
│  └─────────────┘                              │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐            │
│  │ InsightFace │  │ ANPR        │            │
│  │ (FRS)       │  │ (YOLO+OCR)  │            │
│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘            │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐            │
│  │ Virtual     │  │ Anomaly /   │            │
│  │ Fence ROI   │  │ Pose Engine │            │
│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘            │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────┐         │
│  │ Night Vision Enhancer (CLAHE+)  │         │
│  └─────────────────────────────────┘         │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────┘
        │
        ▼
[Alert Engine] → WebSocket push → [React Dashboard]
[Event Logger] → PostgreSQL → [Command API REST endpoint]
```

