## SECTION 3: EXISTING SOLUTIONS & THEIR LIMITATIONS

### 3.1 Commercial Platforms

#### Hikvision AcuSense + Deep Learning Cameras
| Feature | Capability | Limitation |
|---------|-----------|------------|
| Human/vehicle detection | ✅ Excellent | ❌ Requires Hikvision-specific cameras |
| ANPR | ✅ Available | ❌ Separate hardware module required |
| FRS | ✅ Available | ❌ External FRS server = $50K+ |
| Cost | High ($500-2000/camera) | ❌ Not software-only |
| Vendor lock-in | Full lock-in | ❌ Can't use with non-HIK cameras |
| India deployment | Available | ❌ Data sovereignty concerns (Chinese HW) |

**Why IBVAP wins against it:** IBVAP works with ANY existing camera.
BSF already has cameras. No hardware replacement = ₹0 hardware cost.

#### Genetec Security Center + Mission Control
| Feature | Capability | Limitation |
|---------|-----------|------------|
| Integration | ✅ Exceptional | ❌ $200K+ licensing |
| Scalability | ✅ Enterprise-grade | ❌ Overkill for border BOPs |
| Analytics | ✅ Comprehensive | ❌ US company, sovereignty concern |
| Custom AI | ❌ Limited | ❌ Can't add custom models |

#### BriefCam (SYNOPSIS Engine)
| Feature | Capability | Limitation |
|---------|-----------|------------|
| Video summaries | ✅ Excellent | ❌ Forensic (post-event) not real-time |
| Search | ✅ Face/object search | ❌ No real-time border alert |
| Cost | Very expensive | ❌ Not built for border requirements |

#### Dahua WizMind AI Cameras
Same limitations as Hikvision. Chinese hardware = deployment concern for India's
sensitive border infrastructure.

---

### 3.2 Open Source Solutions

#### Frigate NVR (Home Surveillance)
- ✅ Free, good detection using YOLOv8
- ❌ Built for home use, no ANPR/FRS/military-grade features
- ❌ No alert API, no centralized command integration
- ❌ Can't handle multi-site deployment

#### OpenALPR / ALPR Cloud (ANPR Only)
- ✅ Good Indian plate support
- ❌ ANPR only, no broader surveillance features
- ❌ Cloud-based version has privacy issues

#### DeepStack (AI Server)
- ✅ Easy API for running AI models locally
- ❌ Not a surveillance platform, no streaming support
- ❌ No tracking, no alert management

#### OpenCV-based Custom Solutions (Research Code)
- ✅ Full control, MIT license
- ❌ No production hardening, no UI, no alert management
- ❌ Requires months of engineering to productionize

**IBVAP's position:** Fills the gap between home surveillance tools (too simple)
and enterprise commercial platforms (too expensive, not sovereign).

