## SECTION 9: 36-HOUR TEAM EXECUTION PLAN

### Team of 6 — Parallel Tracks

```
HOURS 0-2: ALL TOGETHER
  ✅ Set up GitHub repo, Docker environment
  ✅ Download datasets (MOT17 for tracker test, Indian LP for ANPR)
  ✅ Install: ultralytics, insightface, easyocr, mediapipe, faiss-cpu, fastapi

HOURS 2-14: SPLIT INTO 3 PAIRS

Pair 1 (Detection + Tracking):
  ✅ Build CameraStream class (RTSP + file mode)
  ✅ Integrate YOLOv8n + ByteTrack
  ✅ Implement virtual fence (shapely polygon logic)
  ✅ Implement loitering detection (time-based)
  ✅ Night enhancement (CLAHE pipeline)
  Deliverable: Script that reads video → detects + tracks → produces annotated output

Pair 2 (ANPR + FRS):
  ✅ Fine-tune / test YOLOv8 on license plate dataset (Colab GPU)
  ✅ EasyOCR pipeline with regex post-processing
  ✅ InsightFace pipeline with FAISS enrollments
  ✅ Liveness detection with MiniFASNet
  Deliverable: ANPR script + FRS script that process image → return reading/match

Pair 3 (Backend + Frontend):
  ✅ FastAPI backend with endpoints: /stream, /alerts, /enroll, /fence-config
  ✅ WebSocket push for real-time alerts
  ✅ PostgreSQL schema: cameras, alerts, watchlist, fences
  ✅ React dashboard: live video, alert panel, camera map, alert history
  Deliverable: Working dashboard with mock data, WebSocket connected

HOURS 14-24: INTEGRATION
  ✅ Wire Pair 1 detection events → Pair 3 alert API
  ✅ Wire Pair 2 ANPR + FRS results → Pair 3 alert API
  ✅ End-to-end test with pre-recorded video
  ✅ Debug integration issues

HOURS 24-30: POLISH + DEMO PREP
  ✅ Record demo video as backup
  ✅ Fix critical bugs only (don't add new features)
  ✅ Pre-enroll faces for FRS demo
  ✅ Calibrate virtual fence for demo camera/video

HOURS 30-36: PRESENTATION
  ✅ Write evaluation summary (accuracy numbers per module)
  ✅ Prepare 6-slide technical deck
  ✅ Rehearse demo narration
  ✅ Deployment cost comparison slide (IBVAP vs Hikvision investment)
```

